download_bytes=sum(x.get('archive_bytes',x.get('csv_bytes',0)) for x in src['sources']);parquet_bytes=sum(x['parquet_bytes'] for x in src['sources']);all_rows=sum(x['source_rows'] for x in src['sources'] if 'month'in x)
scale=f"The measured ingestion scanned **{all_rows:,} all reporting-carrier source rows**, retaining **{w['counts']['flights']:,} WN flights**. Eight stations supplied **{w['counts']['raw_weather']:,} source reports**, deduplicated to **{w['counts']['stg_weather']:,} observations**. The warehouse creates **{w['counts']['features']:,} hourly feature rows** and **{w['counts']['rotations']:,} validated retrospective links**.\n\nOriginal downloads totaled **{download_bytes:,} bytes**; scoped flight/weather Parquet totaled **{parquet_bytes:,} bytes**. Stage wall times on the development Mac were ingestion **{src['ingest_wall_seconds']:.1f}s** (initial download), full warehouse **{w['seconds']:.1f}s**, model evaluation **{m['runtime_seconds']:.1f}s**, and recovery evaluation **{s['runtime_seconds']:.1f}s**. These are separately observed local stage measurements, with cache/host effects, not a throughput guarantee or a single uninterrupted end-to-end timing.\n\nA January eight-airport weather query compares range-join-plus-ranking with ASOF. Both return the same SHA-256 result. Three fresh-connection repetitions measured **{b['speedup']:.1f}×** median speedup and **{100*b['buffer_memory_reduction']:.1f}%** lower DuckDB peak buffer memory. This is a subset improvement; buffer memory is not process RSS. Inspect [before/after SQL](sql), [EXPLAIN/profile evidence](reports/query_benchmark.json) and [warehouse measurements](reports/warehouse_run.json)."
